{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## D(24|28|274|72[2-9]|73[0-9])'\"\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n '\"'^##|send|evidence|run-rate'\"' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/{design,RESULT}.md; rg -n 'implied_outcome|reference' src/hivemind/{bundle.py,views/bundle.py,service.py}\"","aggregated_output":"433:## D24 · 2026-10-16 · Financial reports are not streamed; pull mode reads them when a thesis needs them\n567:## D28 · 2026-10-18 · Financial reports stream again\n3151:## D274 · 2026-11-03 · The extraction production prompt is frozen at v74i (`poc-v108`); the unadopted variants are retired\n10892:## D722 · 2026-11-22 · Alex closes the double-count design with nothing changed\n10905:## D723 · 2026-11-22 · Code review of 95cf8da7..3ba40d8f: two defects fixed, eight findings recorded\n10931:## D724 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 44 converges the code review: keep the v12 launcher refusal and the clean-ups, revert the link-step catch; D723 corrected\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/RESULT.md:6:## What was sent\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/RESULT.md:7:old-2's v9 (FY2027 Data Center revenue) at 09-20, six fresh samples (`probe.py send`, `send.log`, `run/answers.jsonl`):\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/RESULT.md:12:## Result\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/RESULT.md:21:## What it does not show\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/RESULT.md:31:## Next (registered, consensus)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/RESULT.md:33:D538's seven filing changes (a link can remove evidence from the company-wide question). Trace the self-made reference on stored\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md:1:# Council Q, round 3: the dependency probe's design, before any send (read-only; no edits, no model calls)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md:3:## Alex's word\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md:7:## What I found since round 2 (read these)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md:29:## The probe (`probe.py send`)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md:32:  each in its own empty archive (fresh samples), a refused answer retried once with production's note. 18 sends, about $0.006 each\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md:36:## Reading, written before any answer\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md:37:For every answer, I and a blind reader (you, given answers under shuffled labels with the total's shown conclusion and the evidence\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md:39:evidence or to the dependency; whether it relates its figure to the total.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md:48:## Questions\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/design.md:52:- (c) Anything to change before the send?\nrg: src/hivemind/views/bundle.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '433,450p;567,586p;3151,3166p;10859,10904p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; sed -n '1,100p' docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md; sed -n '1,120p' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/RESULT.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '433,450p;567,586p;3151,3166p;10859,10904p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; sed -n '1,100p' docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md; sed -n '1,120p' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/RESULT.md\"","aggregated_output":"## D24 · 2026-10-16 · Financial reports are not streamed; pull mode reads them when a thesis needs them\n\n- By: Alex (\"这个system的核心是抽取thesis, 所以我在想这样刷财报是真的有意义的吗？\"; on designing the research\n  conclusions first: \"我同意，我们不应该再stream 财报了，这个没有意义。应该是在我们还没设计的pull mode 里面采用。这个记录下来，\n  和我们之前旧版的设计思路有很大的区别\").\n- Why: the system exists to form and test theses, and a thesis is an argued view whose few drivers name the numbers\n  it needs; financial-report lines are evidence, never its definition. Reading every reported number as it streams\n  in builds a store the theses then search, and lets the available numbers shape the theses. The old system's stored\n  data shows it: for three companies it kept 11,841 numbers, of which the theses cited 543 (4.6%); of the 21 KPIs the\n  theses watched, 9 appear in no table at all and none of those 9 got a number.\n- Decides: financial reports are not part of the stream. When a thesis's ladder or evidence needs a number from a\n  report (for example \"if Apple's iPhone revenue turns negative year over year next quarter, the view fails\"), pull\n  mode fetches that number at the due date and checks it. Stream mode keeps the items that move theses as they arrive.\n  The research conclusions (thesis, ladder, evidence) are designed next; extraction and the research store follow\n  from what a thesis needs (the fact-path drafts of D23 are paused, not deleted: a number's identity and \"the same\n  value again is a confirmation\" may be reused).\n- Differs from the old system: the old system fetched each company's whole financial statements on every refresh\n  (provider statements plus the tables of every 10-Q/10-K), kept every line and its derived growth, and offered the\n## D28 · 2026-10-18 · Financial reports stream again\n\n- By: Alex (\"我觉得新的财报应该还是可以推进来，但是观点就变成抽取新的 + 验证当前的\").\n- Decides: earnings releases (T1), periodic reports (T2) and earnings calls (T4) are back in the stream; the\n  universe's company default is T1–T10, T12–T15 again and the US–China tariffs example T10, T7, T8, T1–T6. They are\n  read like every other item into views and evidence (D27). D24's thesis-first point stands: no number warehouse.\n- Enforced: `TRACKING_DEFAULTS` and `TRACKING_EXAMPLES` of `docs/system-design/new-universe.js`; the universe node of\n  `docs/system-design/new-design.js`; `docs/prd/01-universe.md`.\n\n## D29 · 2026-10-18 · A final verdict before any view is closed\n\n- By: Alex (\"确实让模型完整看一遍再关掉是稳妥的，这边可以多画一个环节block就是来做final verdict\").\n- Decides: a view is closed only by the final verdict, a model call that reads the view, all its evidence, its\n  premise's state and why it was sent. Triggers: a confirm or falsify condition met (code); the due date (pull mode,\n  only after every item published on or before it is processed); the premise's status changed (at once); the premise\n  weakened (at the object's next item, at the latest after 7 days by pull mode); weakening evidence of the \"happened\"\n  tier; a disagreement between independent sources in one tier; a corrected item that removes a view's basis.\n  Outcomes: closed as confirmed or falsified (citing evidence), closed as expired (\"no data to verify\" when no evidence\n  can decide), or kept (a premise removed or replaced, conditions added). Only conditions plus evidence of the\n  \"happened\" tier can close a view. A verdict is a new version of the view with its sources; when a view closes,\n## D274 · 2026-11-03 · The extraction production prompt is frozen at v74i (`poc-v108`); the unadopted variants are retired\n\n- Alex: \"感觉已经瓶颈了，上一个版本是不是freeze作为我们的抽取生产提示词吧。你顺道把所有其他不相关的clean up sanitize吧\". Read as: the last prompt version, v74i (D273's\n  three exceptions narrowed), at low reasoning, the configuration every reasoning test of the third round kept unchanged; it beat the D272 default on core\n  matters, supporting matters and noise on the 50 stored articles (D273 amended). If he meant v74d, the default goes back to `poc-v103` with one line.\n- Frozen: `poc/config/poc-v108.json` is the replay default (`scripts/replay.py`, README, AGENTS); `tests/test_frozen_extraction_prompt.py` pins the sha256 of\n  role-v74i, review-v74i, categories-v74i and the configuration, the links rule (`placement.FILING_RULE_ROOT_FALLBACK`, now a constant of its own), the\n  code-written takes lines and the evidence schema; a one-character change to the check fails it (mutant checked). AGENTS \"Where to look first\" names it.\n- Retired, never run as a stored run and never a default, backed up first (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/retired-2026-11-03/retired-variants.tar.gz`,\n  54 files, sha256 manifest beside it, restore verified): prompt files of v74b, v74c, v74e–v74h, v74j, v74k, v76, v77, v78, v79, v80; configurations\n  poc-v96, v97, v98–v102, v104–v107, v109–v114; `tests/test_evidence_fields.py` (the field route's tests leave with it). Code removed with them: the v78–v80\n  classification fields and `evidence_rule` in the sift (and the `>= 78` version gates that would have caught any future version), the section markers\n  of v74j, the variant tables of v74f–v74k; `REVIEW_VERSIONS_ALSO` keeps 72–75. Kept: v94 and v95 (stored runs), v74d / `poc-v103` (D272's default), every\n  research record, proof, saved answer and probe. The request bytes of `poc-v94`, `poc-v95`, `poc-v103` and `poc-v108` on three stored articles are\n  identical before and after the cleanup (sha256 compared). Tests: `test_v74_production_text.py` (v74d and v74i), the review gate test states v76–v80 do\n  not exist; suite 283.\n## D721 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 43/43b: the double-count premise is partly falsified by the frozen gold; recommend closing the design with nothing to build; D711's H4 reading corrected\n\n- **The rounds** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-whole-and-part/`):\n  - **Round 43** (`round43-brief.md`, `codex-r43.md`, `claude-r43.md`): DIAGNOSIS NEEDS CHANGES. old-1 has 26 explicit additions (not\n    32). Six of Claude's became unclear (`1569`, `1691`, `1782`, `2313`, `2907`, `3293`). Codex also found overlapping quarterly\n    adjustments, and argued that D263 supports keeping the target discount.\n  - **Round 43b** (`round43b-brief.md`, `codex-r43b.md`, `claude-r43b.md`): PARTLY.\n- **The check that changed the frame:** the frozen judgement gold (D262).\n  - **q01**, total revenue at 07-14, band $400–435B: the gold builds a second half above consensus. It lists management's \"$20bn of\n    Vera CPU sales by fiscal year-end\" among the supporting inputs, though not among the decisive items, and allocates it no dollar\n    amount.\n  - **q19**, stand-alone Vera: $8–18B.\n  - **What follows:** the diagnosis's premise (\"a company-wide basis formed after the target was published already contains it\") is\n    Claude's own view, not the ruler's. A judge sentence enforcing it, or the opposite, would have no source in the frozen standard\n    (AGENTS §6, §7.1).\n- **What survives, recorded as findings:**\n  - **old-1 `4163`:** about the full $20B is added without volume shown, taking $414B to $434B across $431.2B. That is unsupported by\n    the gold's discounting (q19).\n  - **old-1 `978`:** treats a repeat as new, while acknowledging \"possible consensus inclusion\".\n  - **The judge flips:** linked-1 `8752`, `8756` and `8770` change what the same $387B basis includes, with no explanation.\n  - **v9's unsupported \"outside Data Center\" claim** (`8758`, then `8761`): the estimate moves about $20B, the rung does not.\n  - **Overlapping quarterly adjustments in old-3:** 4 clear (`4298`, `4510`, `5195`, `5369`) and 6 related. No rung change is\n    attributable to the overlap alone.\n- **D711's exploratory H4, corrected:**\n  - linked-1 made \"four unsupported increments, overlap unresolved\", not four proved double counts.\n  - Against the paired control, only 07-15 differs in rung. The control reached about $417B without any CPU addition on 07-16..07-18\n    (`8751`, `8755`, `8757`).\n  - The pilot's registered verdict (inconclusive) is unchanged.\n- **Consensus (Claude and Codex):** close the double-count design with nothing built or sent. The findings above go to Alex as a\n  short list, not as a work order (AGENTS, Authority and scope).\n- **Lesson:** before calling a judge's choice a defect, read the frozen gold's own reasoning on that case. The pilot's harm line and\n  two readers' \"double count\" were written without it.\n\n## D722 · 2026-11-22 · Alex closes the double-count design with nothing changed\n\n- **The question** (after D721): \"'总收入把 CPU 又加一遍'这件事，按冻结金标的推理不算错：金标自己就把 CPU 目标当成总收入超过共识的理由之一。我和 Codex 都建议把这个修法设计收尾，什么都不改。你怎么定？\"\n  Options:\n  - 收尾，不改 (recommended: poc-v118 stays, the judge text unchanged, the findings recorded but not worked on, no spend);\n  - 改查 CPU 题估高 (stand-alone CPU near $19.5B against the gold's $8–18B, a $0 diagnosis);\n  - 改查季度叠加 (old-3's overlapping quarterly adjustments, a $0 count).\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22): \"收尾，不改 (推荐)\".\n- **Effect:**\n  - poc-v118 remains the product and no judge version is opened.\n  - D721's findings stay a list, not a work order.\n  - Nothing is queued or being spent.\n\n# A sharpened link question, version 2 (D703; for council review before its cents probe)\n\nAlex chose to probe a sharpened wording before the paid run (D703): keep Data Center reads total revenue and the 38 negatives, remove\nunsupported links including the base effect, no blanket ban on a whole reading its part. The probe is harness-only: `window_test.py\nprobe-v2` replaces the READS and SIGN criteria texts in memory for its pass; no product file changes until a version is chosen.\n\n## 1. Prompt audit (the census's failure classes against the request sentences; AGENTS §6)\n\n| Failure class (census, `CENSUS-RESULT.md`) | The request sentence that produced it | The standard or decision on the case | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Part against whole, direction unsettled: v9–v14 at margins 0.03–0.09; v21–v9 flips between draws; whole-to-part and part-to-whole both occur | READS `candidate_reads_thesis`: \"a part read against its whole (...), or a quantity read against another it depends on (...)\": the second clause lets a whole \"depend on\" its part; no sentence says which reads when both fit | D537: the total carried the year's consensus and guidance that the segment's requests lacked; D260: a judgement is made against what the market expects (consensus, guidance, the stated plan) | **abstract** (two clauses, both directions, no tie-break) |\n| Across periods with an unsupported sign: v17 (FY2028 growth) reads v16 (FY2027 CPU), together, 3 of 3; v35 (FY2028 total) reads v9 (FY2027 Data Center), 1 of 3 | no READS sentence on periods (`neither` covers only \"the same quantity for the same period and scope\"); every SIGN example is within one period | the arithmetic of a growth rate (a higher base lowers next year's growth at a given level); the dependency design §2: another period of the same quantity \"may be linked\" | **missing** |\n\n## 2. The wording (changes marked; every example from another industry, none names the covered company)\n\nREADS, `candidate_reads_thesis`, appended sentence:\n> When either question could be judged with the other in view, the one whose answer the supplied text anchors less (no guidance,\n> consensus or reported figure for the quantity and full period the question asks about) is the one judged with the other's conclusion\n> in view.\n\nREADS, `neither`, appended clause (before \"sharing a company ...\"):\n> or quantities of different periods when the supplied text does not state how one period's answer moves the other's (a retailer's\n> sales this year and its sales growth next year, when the text only names both)\n\nSIGN, `opposite`, added example:\n> ...; one year's sales and the next year's sales growth at a given next-year level, since a higher base lowers the growth\n\n`thesis_reads_candidate` (\"for the same reasons with the roles swapped\") and the instructions are unchanged, so the tie-break applies\nboth ways: a part with guidance and a whole without would have the whole read the part. No direction is banned.\n\nSources (round 18 made the distinction explicit): the general tie-break and the periods clause are proposals this probe is authorized\nto test by D703, not rules already decided; D537 decided only the concrete case (Data Center revenue reading total revenue, the total\ncarrying the year's consensus), and D260 explains why guidance and consensus anchor a judgement (it governs judging, not linking). The\nbase-effect example is the arithmetic of a growth rate with the next-year level held fixed. The periods clause narrows the dependency\ndesign §2 (\"another period of the same quantity may be linked\") to \"when the supplied text states how\": a link across periods still\nexists when the text gives the bridge (v35 reads v14: the FY2028 outlook translates growth into a level through the FY2027 base).\nRound 18 read the seq-148 request (dry archive, call 8744): the total carries Bloomberg's $393B FY2027 estimate, Data Center a Q1\nfigure of $75.25B (92% of the quarter): a full-year anchor against a partial-year one, so the tie-break gives v9 reads v14. Growth: 595\ncharacters across the three criteria texts (READS `candidate_reads_thesis` +269, `neither` +209, SIGN `opposite` +117; the READS\ncriteria repeat in every pair of a job, about 120 tokens a pair); written reason: the audit shows a missing case and an abstract clause, and nothing in the current texts\nduplicates them to cut.\n\n## 3. What the probe decides (registered before its answers: `expected-links-v2.json`)\n\nThe census's registration (R 1, W 38, O 66) with, for version 2 only (`expected-links-v2.json`): **W** for any link across periods\nwhose shown text gives no bridge, the two unsupported links council R named (321:v16, v17 FY2028 growth against v16 FY2027 CPU; 1238:v9,\nv35 FY2028 total against v9 FY2027 Data Center; round 18 showed the gate passing without this); **F**, the base-effect sign, a growth\nrate reading an earlier period's revenue amount with the sign together (321:v8, 321:v9, 321:v14). Version 2: R 1, W 40, O 61, F 3;\n1238:v14 stays O and is reported. Gate: the known positive right in 3 of 3 draws, no W link, no F link. $0 checks on the stored census\nanswers (`scorer-checks.log`): as stored, FAIL on 321:v16 and 1238:v9; with 321:v16 made \"neither\" and 1238:v9 kept, FAIL; with both\nmade \"neither\", PASS; 321:v16 linked with the sign opposite, FAIL; 321:v14 linked together, FAIL. Reported beside: every O pair\nagainst the census, and the margins.\n- **Pass:** version 2 becomes the candidate for the paid design (a product version built and reviewed first).\n- **Fail on the known positive or a W link:** the current wording stays the candidate with its measured risks (D702).\n- **Fail on F only:** the base-effect sentence did not take; reported, the current wording's risk stands.\n- **A ceiling stop before draw 3 completes:** an incomplete probe, no verdict (round 18: the observed job shapes price at about $0.034\n  for three draws; the all-SIGN stress shape at 0.37 tokens a byte at about $0.074 against $0.0734 left).\n\n## 4. The probe\n\n`window_test.py probe-v2 <scratch> <draw> <ledger> 0.10`: the census pass with the version-2 texts patched into `links.READS` and\n`links.SIGN` for the pass; every link job is new (the July answers do not match the new texts), so the seq-148 jobs are bought. Three\ndraws on D700's ledger (spent $0.0266, $0.0734 left); priced as the census (a draw settles about $0.009 at the ledger's rule; the READS\nrequests grow by about 120 tokens a pair). The completeness check, equality with old-2 and the paid-transport record apply as in the\ncensus; `draw.json` records the wording.\n\n## 5. The product version (D705: version 2 as a separately versioned, reviewed configuration)\n\n- **Config:** the matching setting gains `link_questions` (`config.Setting.link_questions`; allowed `links-v1`, `links-v2`), accepted\n  only with the engine `jev-links` (any other engine naming it is refused) and defaulting to `links-v1` there, so `poc-v119.json` is\n  unchanged in bytes, checksum and requests. `poc/config/poc-v120.json` = poc-v119 with `\"link_questions\": \"links-v2\"`.\n- **Code:** `links.py` holds both question sets as literal texts (`READS`, `SIGN` for links-v1; `READS_V2`, `SIGN_V2` for links-v2,\n  byte-equal to the probe's `window_test.wording_v2()`); `reads_question` and `sign_question` take the version; `choose`, `_signed` and\n  `_corrected` pass `cfg.matching.link_questions`. Nothing else reads the field.\n- **Entry points:** unchanged: the ordinary launchers refuse the engine `jev-links` under any question version (D694 §0); poc-v120 runs\n  only in the measurement harness.\n\n| Table | Rows |\n|---|---|\n| Value × reader | `Setting.link_questions`: read by `links.choose`, `_signed`, `_corrected` (searched); indirectly by `parallel_day.environment_key`, which serializes the whole configuration, so a manifest written before the field existed no longer matches and the parallel day refuses it (its existing guard; round 21); `model.build_request` and every other step ignore it. The two text sets: read by the two builders only. Config rule (round 21): named only in matching under `jev-links`, as one of the exact strings; a null or another section is refused; unnamed under `jev-links`, `links-v1`. The harness's `probe-v2` entry points are retired (the builders read `QUESTION_SETS`, so the old patch no longer changes a request). |\n| New path × old checks | poc-v119's link requests byte-equal (the v1 pin `LINK_QUESTIONS_SHA` unchanged; `poc-v119.json` untouched); the v2 texts pinned (`LINK_QUESTIONS_V2_SHA`) and equal to the probe's; poc-v120 over the whole window with the probe's own answers replayed by request hash meets every link job of the probe (READS and SIGN) and ends equal to old-2 (`window_test.py v120-replay`); config refuses an unknown question version and the field on another engine. |\n| State × event | a run keeps one configuration (as for v118/v119, DESIGN.md §0); a store written under poc-v120 and opened under poc-v119 or poc-v118 is read the same (the written rows do not carry the question version; the selection record carries the config checksum); a configuration changed between days is the defined outcome of D694 §0, not a supported mode. |\n| Prior decisions | D359 (a configuration naming a version the code does not build is refused), D694 §0 (entry points), D695, D703, D705. |\n# Dependency probe: does linking reconcile the Data Center answer with total revenue? (Alex's A, D691; 2026-11-20; $0.0176)\n\n**PASS by the registered rule** (`reading-rule.md`, fixed before any answer; council rounds 3–7 in this folder, thread\n`01a1fba6-8066-7031-9a26-da22b7dcbd3d`, consensus in rounds 6 and 7).\n\n## What was sent\nold-2's v9 (FY2027 Data Center revenue) at 09-20, six fresh samples (`probe.py send`, `send.log`, `run/answers.jsonl`):\n- control: the stored request, rebuilt byte-equal through production code (`check.txt`);\n- changed: the same request plus v14's (FY2027 total revenue) 09-20 conclusion through one dependency, rendered by production code.\nold-1 and old-3 were not sent: their rendered link loses the decisive figure at the 600-character cut (`render-check.json`).\n\n## Result\n| Arm | Reconcile (A–D all hold) | Q4 Data Center | Room left for the rest of NVIDIA in Q4 (midpoint) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| changed | 2 of 3 (samples 1 and 3 used v14's $127B Q4 times the reported 92.5% mix; sample 2 only noticed v14) | $117.5B, $118B, $120–125B | $9.5B, $9B, $4.5B |\n| control | 0 of 3 (each sizes Q4 with an unquantified \"acceleration\") | $120–126B, $125–130B, $125–130B | $4B, −$0.5B, −$0.5B |\n\nClaude's marks (`claude-marks.md`, first) and a fresh blind Codex reader (`codex-blind.md`) agree on every answer; key outside the\nrepo (`~/.hivemind-keys/dependency-probe-2026-11-20/key.json`). No refusal in either arm.\n\n## What it does not show\n- **The stored extreme did not recur.** All six answers are rung 3 at $382–394B; none repeats the stored rung 2, about $410B, Q4\n  $146B. Six samples leave that error's frequency unknown. The recurring problem is milder: a Q4 Data Center at or near the whole\n  company's Q4.\n- **Coherence is not accuracy:** the passing answers inherit v14's own assumption (Q4 at Q3's 12% growth) and carry the latest\n  segment share forward.\n- **One draw, one pair.** Linking was not tested in the root-reads-driver direction or on any other pair.\n- **The self-made reference is a separate live defect:** five of six answers still call the $414B (v9's own estimate of 09-12/13)\n  \"the market reference\", one of them a reconciling answer.\n\n## Next (registered, consensus)\nReopen the dependency design review at $0 with the council, then Alex: D542's five open items, the `reads`/`supports` separation, and\nD538's seven filing changes (a link can remove evidence from the company-wide question). Trace the self-made reference on stored\nanswers apart, at $0. The daily wrapper stays deferred; council Q's PARTLY stands.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
